  "id": "gaojia_opera",
  "name": "Gaojiaxi (Gaojia opera of southern Fujian)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Minnan-language opera of Quanzhou, Xiamen and Jinjiang that grew from 'Song Jiang' processional plays of the Ming and Qing into a full theatre famed for its comic chou roles, including clowns who mimic marionettes; it is on China's national intangible heritage list (2006) and is performed in Taiwan and the Minnan communities of Southeast Asia. Its music joins nanyin-derived arias with livelier puppet-theatre and beiguan tunes, accompanied by a shawm, drum, gong and cymbal section alongside pipa and fiddle.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-2000s gaojiaxi, art Music, east Asian branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. rosewood bodied copper belled suona, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, opera bending gong tamtam, naobo, pipa, bamboo stick horsehair threaded between strings erhu. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
